  "story": "A lighthouse keeper logs the ships that pass each night, but only on the nights he stays awake: awake holds 1 for a night he is awake and 0 for a night he dozes off, and ships holds how many ships pass that night, logged or not. One strong coffee keeps him awake for k nights in a row, and he has exactly one. If he drinks it on the best night, what is the largest number of ships he can log in all?",
  "io": {
    "inputs": [
      {"name": "ships", "type": "array<num>"},
      {"name": "awake", "type": "array<num>"},
      {"name": "k", "type": "num"}
    ],
    "output": {"type": "num"}
  },
  "constraints": {
    "n": {"min": 1, "max": 200},
    "notes": ["1 to 200 nights with 0 to 50 ships each; the two lists are equally long.", "k is at least 1 and at most the number of nights."]
  },
  "blocks": {
    "allow": ["arith.add", "arith.max", "arith.min", "arith.sub", "arr.get", "arr.len", "cmp.eq", "cmp.ge", "cmp.gt", "cmp.le", "cmp.lt", "cmp.ne", "ctrl.break", "ctrl.else", "ctrl.for_range", "ctrl.foreach", "ctrl.if", "ctrl.return", "ctrl.while", "lit.num", "logic.and", "logic.not", "logic.or", "var.dec", "var.get", "var.inc", "var.set"],
    "maxBlocks": 92
  },
  "limits": {"maxOps": 13250, "maxDepth": 32, "maxAlloc": 100},
  "hints": ["Ships on nights he is awake anyway are logged whatever he does. The coffee only adds the ships of the dozing nights it covers.", "So find the run of k nights with the most ships on dozing nights. Slide the run one night at a time: add the night that enters, take away the night that leaves, and count a night only when awake is 0.", "In one FOR over the nights keep three numbers: the ships logged anyway, the extra ships of the current run, and the MAX extra seen. A night leaves the run when the position is GREATER OR EQUAL to k. RETURN the first PLUS the third."],
  "validators": {"output": "equal"},
